{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"🚨 **BLOCKING: `_rebuildAllRequests` still drops the running cumulative — the bulk/CLI path reports per-request usage as the cumulative (re-review of head `9d34bb98e`; still failing)**

Re-reviewed the current head `9d34bb98e`. The head moved only by merging `main` into the branch — **the fix for this thread was never pushed** and the code is byte-for-byte the reviewed state. The loop still seeds every fold with `null` and discards the return value:

```dart
for (var i = 0; i < facts.length; i++) {
  _reqPositions[facts[i]] = i;
  _foldRequestNumber(i, facts[i], null);   // ← running cumulative lost
}
```

**Verified locally at `9d34bb98e`** — the failing CI test still fails:

```
dart test test/integration/trajectory/cli_integration_test.dart --plain-name "cost prints the usage table with the cumulative line"
Expected: contains 'session cumulative: in 400'
Actual:   '...session cumulative: in 200, out 40, tokens 240, cost $0.0300'
```

This is the fallback derivation `appendAll` always takes (single publish, `_reqSorted == null`), so the `fa trajectory cost` CLI / session-open path returns wrong cumulative usage. The one-line fix from the previous round (verified locally: all `test/trajectory/` tests pass and the integration test goes green):

```dart
_reqCumulative = <Usage?>[];
Usage? cumulative;
for (var i = 0; i < facts.length; i++) {
  _reqPositions[facts[i]] = i;
  cumulative = _foldRequestNumber(i, facts[i], cumulative);
}
```

The doc comment above this method still claims "byte-identical to the pre-#1497 code" — with the fix it actually becomes true. Also note the regression test requested alongside this (see the sibling comment on the test file) is still the single-fact version, which passes even with this bug.
"}

{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the bulk-replay regression test still uses a single request fact — it cannot catch the broken cumulative fold (re-review; unchanged at head `9d34bb98e`)**

This test still asserts `bulk.requests.single.cumulativeUsage?.totalTokens == 15`. With exactly one usage-carrying fact, "cumulative" and "own usage" are indistinguishable — the test passes even while `_rebuildAllRequests` seeds every row from `null` (the blocking bug on this PR, still present and still red in `PTY/CLI integration`). A regression guard that cannot fail while the guarded bug is live is not a guard.

Extend it to at least two usage-carrying assistant facts (e.g. 15 then 20 tokens) and assert the second request's cumulative is the **sum** (35), plus the same expectations on the per-append `live` builder so both publish paths are pinned:

```dart
expect(bulk.requests[1].cumulativeUsage?.totalTokens, 35);
expect(liveSnapshot.requests[1].cumulativeUsage?.totalTokens, 35);
```

A multi-fact version of this test fails on the current head and passes with the one-line `_rebuildAllRequests` fix.
"}

